meta {
  name: 27 Print All Reports
  type: http
  seq: 27
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/order/{{orderId}}/print-all
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {}
}

tests {
  test("200 or 201 with a PDF", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]);
    expect(res.getHeader("content-type")).to.include("application/pdf");
  });
}

docs {
  Print All (order-console's "Lab All Report" action). Renders ONE
  `lab_all_report`-type template, flattening every one of the order's lab
  reports' result rows into a single `sections.results` array so the body
  reads as one continuous report, test by test. Streams the rendered PDF
  directly (`Content-Type: application/pdf`).

  Declared before the `:id` routes on the controller (same convention as
  `tat/summary`), so `order` in the URL is never captured as a report id.

  ## Body

  - `templateId` — optional. Omit to use the tenant's single active
    `lab_all_report` template. Required if more than one exists.
  - No `type` field — this action's type is always `lab_all_report`.

  ## Resolution & errors

  - 404 `ORDER_REPORTS_NOT_FOUND` — the order has no `LabReport` rows at all
    (wrong id, or no item has reached ACCEPTED yet).
  - 404 `NO_ACTIVE_PRINT_TEMPLATE` — no active `lab_all_report` template
    exists for the tenant.
  - 409 `AMBIGUOUS_PRINT_TEMPLATE` — more than one active `lab_all_report`
    template and no `templateId` given.

  ## Render context

  `variables` — taken from the FIRST report's context (order/patient data is
  identical across every report on the same order, so this is safe): same
  field set as `26 Print Report`'s `lab_report` variables.

  `sections.results` — flattened across every report on the order. Each row
  carries its own `test_name` (re-injected per row, on top of the single-print
  row shape) plus `parameter_name`, `observed1`, `observed2`, `unit`,
  `methodology`, `reference_display`. A report with zero result rows still
  gets ONE placeholder row (`test_name` set, everything else `""`) so it isn't
  silently dropped from the consolidated document — e.g. an order item whose
  report was never entered.

  `signatories` — taken from the first report's signatories only (same
  conditional-empty-array rule as `26 Print Report`).
}
